{"term":"undertake","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:afcc107c4584a154dd","definition":"To take upon oneself; to start, to embark on.","example":"They undertook the new venture, not sure where it would lead.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["tackle","take on","set about"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2590a1cf8c24e9aead","definition":"To commit oneself (to an obligation, activity etc.).","example":"He undertook to exercise more in future.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:26f6b1d8d27a5e1d75","definition":"To pass a slower moving vehicle on the curbside rather than on the side closest to oncoming traffic.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["overtake"],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, informal","register":"UK, informal","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f329e921e9523b3f38","definition":"To pledge; to assert, assure; to dare say.","example":"That is her ransom; I deliver her;\nAnd those two counties I will undertake\nYour grace shall well and quietly enjoy.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, intransitive","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:abde9ed7a9d754a43e","definition":"To take by trickery; to trap, to seize upon.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete, transitive","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8a0c95bfbcd03b57c9","definition":"To assume, as a character; to take on.","example":"Quince. […] you must needs play Pyramus.\nBottom. Well, I will undertake it.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:db38d1605c6b894c97","definition":"To engage with; to attack, take on in a fight.","example":"It is not fit your lordship should undertake every companion that you give offence to.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:964b945b6e7aebd1e0","definition":"To have knowledge of; to hear.","example":"Ne he his mouth would open unto wight,\nUntill that Guyon selfe unto him spake,\nAnd called Brigadore, (so was he hight,)\nWhose voice so soone as he did undertake,\nEftsoones he stood as still as any stake,","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f2797b2fe1672602fb","definition":"To have or take charge of.","example":"To the water side I must conduct your grace;\nThen give my charge up to Sir Nicholas Vaux,\nWho undertakes you to your end.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c7e366dff8bcb923de","definition":"The passing of slower traffic on the curbside rather than on the side closest to oncoming traffic.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["overtake"],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, informal","register":"UK, informal","wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/undertake#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˌʌndəˈteɪk/"},"wordFamily":["reundertake","undertakable","undertakement","undertaker","undertaking"]}